---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, commands, files, env } from '../../data/site';
const toc = [
  ['name', 'Name'], ['synopsis', 'Synopsis'], ['description', 'Description'], ['commands', 'Stages'],
  ['files', 'Files'], ['environment', 'Environment'], ['exit-status', 'Exit status'], ['see-also', 'See also'],
];
---
<Base title="Manual" description="The onigami manual: the pipeline stages, their tools, the files and the environment variables for the agentic red-team crew that runs on your terminal.">
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" data-well="manual" class="man">
    <header class="man__head">
      <p class="man__strip" aria-hidden="true"><span>ONIGAMI(1)</span><span>General Commands Manual</span><span>ONIGAMI(1)</span></p>
      <h1 class="man__title" data-split="chars" data-intro>onigami(1)</h1>
      <p class="man__lede" data-split="lines" data-intro data-delay="0.2">The reference for onigami {site.version}: one binary, one pipeline, a crew of agents. Run it with <code>--tui</code> for the live dashboard.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="man__body">
      <nav class="man__toc" data-toc aria-label="On this page">
        <ol>
          {toc.map(([id, label]) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a></li>)}
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <article class="man__doc">
        <section id="name" class="man__sec">
          <h2 class="man__h">Name</h2>
          <p><strong>onigami</strong>: run a crew of AI agents against a target you are authorized to test, and prove what it finds.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="synopsis" class="man__sec">
          <h2 class="man__h">Synopsis</h2>
          <pre class="term man__pre">{`SCOPE=TARGET onigami --mission "OBJECTIVE" [--tui] [--llm-orch]`}</pre>
        </section>
        <section id="description" class="man__sec">
          <h2 class="man__h">Description</h2>
          <p>onigami runs one engagement as a fixed pipeline: recon, then web testing, then triage, then a proof-of-concept, and, when Metasploit is wired up, a gated demonstration. A long-lived orchestrator plans; ephemeral workers do the work. Scope is enforced in code, not in a prompt.</p>
          <p>Facts come from tools, not from the model. The mechanical steps run as code and record what a real scanner or the CVE databases returned; an agent's own claim is kept apart and never acted on. The model reasons over those facts and writes the report. See <a class="i-link" href="#files">Files</a>.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="commands" class="man__sec">
          <h2 class="man__h">Stages</h2>
          {commands.map((c) => (
            <div class="man__cmd" id={c.name}>
              <h3 class="man__cmdname"><span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">▸ </span>{c.name}</h3>
              <pre class="term man__syn">{c.synopsis}</pre>
              {c.detail.map((d) => <p>{d}</p>)}
              <dl class="man__opts">
                {c.options.map(([k, v]) => (<><dt><code>{k}</code></dt><dd>{v}</dd></>))}
              </dl>
            </div>
          ))}
        </section>
        <section id="files" class="man__sec">
          <h2 class="man__h">Files</h2>
          <dl class="man__opts">{files.map(([k, v]) => (<><dt><code>{k}</code></dt><dd>{v}</dd></>))}</dl>
        </section>
        <section id="environment" class="man__sec">
          <h2 class="man__h">Environment</h2>
          <dl class="man__opts">{env.map(([k, v]) => (<><dt><code>{k}</code></dt><dd>{v}</dd></>))}</dl>
        </section>
        <section id="exit-status" class="man__sec">
          <h2 class="man__h">Exit status</h2>
          <dl class="man__opts">
            <dt><code>0</code></dt><dd>the engagement completed; a report was written</dd>
            <dt><code>1</code></dt><dd>the run ended early (no scope or mission, a rate limit, or a give-up); findings so far are still reported</dd>
          </dl>
        </section>
        <section id="see-also" class="man__sec">
          <h2 class="man__h">See also</h2>
          <p><code>nmap(1)</code>, <code>sqlmap(1)</code>, <code>nuclei(1)</code>, <code>ffuf(1)</code>, <code>msfconsole(1)</code>. Source and issues on <a class="i-link" href={site.github} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.</p>
          <p class="man__strip man__strip--end" aria-hidden="true"><span>onigami {site.version}</span><span>October 2026</span><span>ONIGAMI(1)</span></p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
